From: Baihui Liang (as posted to dri-devel, July 2026; v3 of "drm/imagination: support GPU on SpacemiT K3")
Subject: [PATCH] drm/imagination: allow probe when no power-domains are described

On SpacemiT K3 the GPU power domain is enabled by the boot loader before
Linux runs and is not managed by Linux, so the device tree describes no
power-domains. of_count_phandle_with_args() then returns -ENOENT, which made
the probe fail. Treat a missing property as "no domain to attach".

Backported to v7.2.6 for the Omarchy K3 port; the upstream series is in review.
---
--- a/pvr_power.c
+++ b/pvr_power.c
@@ -635,6 +635,15 @@
 
 	domain_count = of_count_phandle_with_args(dev->of_node, "power-domains",
 						  "#power-domain-cells");
+	if (domain_count == -ENOENT) {
+		/*
+		 * No "power-domains" property in the device tree: the platform
+		 * handles power domains transparently or at the firmware/bootloader
+		 * level, so there is no domain to attach. Treat this as non-fatal.
+		 */
+		err = 0;
+		goto out;
+	}
 	if (domain_count < 0) {
 		err = domain_count;
 		goto out;
